          "website": {
            "url": "",
            "label": "",
            "inlineLink": false
          },
          "description": "<ul><li>Raised warranty coverage from 16% to 95% of labor events (target: 85%) and eliminated $4M in physical time study labor with a TensorFlow ordinal deep-learning model predicting equipment repair times, reaching 98% exact-class accuracy on the holdout set.</li><li>Replaced a regression model (R² 0.54) using sentence transformer embeddings of labor descriptions across 2M+ combinations of labor code, sales model, and build variant.</li><li>Found warranty labor times were censored at the published standard and excluded them, building ground truth from time studies, engineering estimates, and outlier-trimmed non-warranty medians instead of inheriting flawed labels.</li><li>Governed the model with an explicit abstention rule (no prediction on unseen build variants or job codes) and per-segment validation gates at a 90% floor.</li><li>Delivered in one month a parts revenue forecast across 156 global dealers that two prior attempts over two years had not produced: a time series decomposition neural network forecasting parts dollars per technician at 3% MAPE, separating trend, seasonality, and residual.</li><li>Embedded a clustering model in Power BI to track dealer trends over time, giving Caterpillar a basis to engage dealers on service operations, marketing, and training programs.</li></ul><p><strong>Stack:</strong> Python, R, SQL · PyTorch, TensorFlow/Keras, XGBoost, scikit-learn · Snowflake · AWS (SageMaker, Glue, Athena, Lambda, Step Functions, ECS/EKS, CloudWatch) · Docker · Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions</p>",
          "roles": []
        },
